      "title": [
        "Tobakspipa, pipa"
      ],
      "dcDescription": [
        "Tobakspipa.\nFrom Motu people of the Central Division. The cigarette (of dry leaf containing tobacco) is put in the small hole in the side of the tube. The smoker draws the smoke into the tube by placing his mouth over the hole in the end. The cigarette is then removed and the smoke drawn into the lungs from the small hole. The decoration is \"poker-work\". A sliver of casuarina pine is used for the \"poker\". It is kept aglow by blowing on it continually as the artist traces his patterns. 1936.32.0042 Central Division, Brittiska Nya Guinea  Papua C.E 09-84 Central Division, Brit.Nya Guinea. [[Haga"
